.TH ORO-APPLICATION-UPDATE 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:application/update \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:application/update'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
High\-level helpers for fetching and verifying signed application updates.
.PP
The wire format and transport bindings are described in `docs/APPLICATION_UPDATE_PROTOCOL.md`. This module focuses on the client side: downloading manifests and artifacts, verifying signatures and hashes, and selecting suitable updates for the current platform.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBselectUpdate(manifest, options)\fR
Selects a suitable update for the given options.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fImanifest\fR (UpdateManifest; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (UpdateSelectionOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIUpdateSelectionResult \\| null\fR
.TP
\fBverifyArtifact(payload, target)\fR
Verifies an artifact payload against the hash declared in the target.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpayload\fR (Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer; required)
.br
\fItarget\fR (UpdateTarget; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBopenArtifactArchive(artifact)\fR
Opens a verified artifact as a tar archive using the native tar service. This is a convenience helper that wraps the artifact bytes in a TarArchive so callers can inspect and extract entries using the `oro:tar` API surface.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIartifact\fR (Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer \\| import('../buffer.js').Buffer; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<import('../tar.js').TarArchive>\fR
.TP
\fBdownloadUpdate(target, options)\fR
Downloads an artifact and verifies its hash. Prefers the native update service and falls back to the JS fetch\-based implementation when the service is not available in this build.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItarget\fR (UpdateTarget; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (DownloadOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Uint8Array>\fR
.TP
\fBfetchManifest(options)\fR
Fetches and verifies a manifest + signature pair.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ManifestFetchOptions; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<{ manifest: UpdateManifest, raw: Uint8Array, signature: ManifestSignature }>\fR
.TP
\fBcheckForUpdates(options)\fR
High\-level helper: fetches & verifies the manifest, selects an update, and optionally downloads the artifact. Prefers the native update(service) when available and falls back to the JS implementation otherwise.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (UpdateCheckOptions; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<UpdateCheckResult>\fR
